# Two requests in one Session

## Section

The Agent retains a portable `Jido.Session` in `:messages`. The second model
request can see the first completed exchange. Change `backend` to `:live` and
set `OPENAI_API_KEY` to use the same Agent with a real model.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

script = [
  %{reply: {:text, "The case code is ALPHA."}},
  %{reply: {:text, "The code is ALPHA."}}
]

mock = if backend == :mock, do: elem(Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: script), 1)
context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Declare retained Context

```elixir
defmodule Guide.TwoRequests do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_two_requests"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{
      reply: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default(""),
      messages: Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.schema()
    })

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Use the prior completed conversation when it helps."
      memory history: :messages

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 1
      end

      result into: :reply
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.two_requests", ai: :assistant
  end
end
```

## Ask twice

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.TwoRequests, id: "guide-two-requests")

{:ok, first} =
  Guide.TwoRequests.ask_sync(server, "Remember that the case code is ALPHA.", context: context)

{:ok, second} = Guide.TwoRequests.ask_sync(server, "What is the case code?", context: context)

session = Jido.AgentServer.agent(server).state.messages
{:ok, selected} = Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.select(session)
{:ok, messages} = Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.messages(selected)

%{first: first, second: second, session_id: session.id, selected_roles: Enum.map(messages, & &1.role)}
```

The raw Thread can contain more than the selected model messages. Mock mode
checks that the second provider request contains the first case code.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [_, second_request]} =
    Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)

  true = String.contains?(Jason.encode!(second_request.body), "ALPHA")
end
```

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Session, Thread, and Context](../v3/17_session_thread_context.md).
